  "text": "## Q1 2026 Compliance Bulletins  \n### Bulletin #1: Enhanced KYC Requirements Effective March 1, 2026  \n**Date Issued:** 2026-01-20\n**Effective:** 2026-03-01\n**Audience:** All Customer-Facing Staff, Compliance  \n**Summary:**\nFCA has issued enhanced guidance on Know Your Customer (KYC) procedures for high-risk customers. All staff must be aware of new requirements before March 1, 2026.  \n**Key Changes:**\n1. **Beneficial Ownership:** If customer is a company/trust, we must verify actual owners (>25% ownership)\n2. **Source of Funds:** Large deposits (>£10,000) require explanation of where money came from\n3. **Enhanced Monitoring:** High-risk customers (PEP, foreign, high-value) reviewed quarterly not annually  \n**Your Responsibility:**\n- If opening account, collect source of funds info for large deposits\n- If customer is company, ask about real owners\n- Flag any unclear ownership structures to Compliance\n- Ask customer where money is coming from (friendly, non-suspicious tone)  \n**Example Scenarios:**\n- Customer opens account with £50,000 deposit\n- Ask: \"Where is this deposit coming from?\" (salary, savings, business, inheritance?)\n- Verify: Request recent payslip, savings statement, or business accounts  \n- Customer is limited company\n- Ask: \"Who are the beneficial owners of this company?\"\n- Verify: Request shareholders list, director information  \n**Training:** Mandatory training session Friday, February 15, 2026 (90 minutes)\n**Questions:** Email compliance@firstuk.bank  \n---",
